[I] Embeddable Common Lisp

[T] ECL (Embeddable Common-Lisp) is an ANSI Common Lisp implementation that
[T] includes a Lisp to C compiler producing static or shared libraries
[T] callable from C. It can build standalone executables and can itself be
[T] linked into programs as a shared library, with an interpreter for use
[T] without a C compiler.

[U] https://ecl.common-lisp.dev/

[A] Ecl Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base

[V] 26.5.5
[L] LGPL

